[node name="HowToText" type="RichTextLabel" parent="MarginContainer/ScrollContainer/Main_VBoxContainer/Popups_Container/DevAgentPopup/DevAgentPopupVBox/DevAgentMargin/DevAgentScroll/DevAgentTabs/HowTo" unique_id=482140520]
layout_mode = 2
size_flags_horizontal = 3
size_flags_vertical = 3
bbcode_enabled = true
text = "[b]What Dev Agent is[/b]
Dev Agent is SynTree's developer mode: it gives the AI model controlled agency to make real project changes and run the harness.

[b]How it's set up in SynTree / Synesyn[/b]
- You provide [i]scope[/i] via Active Sources (files the agent is allowed to work in).
- You control [i]side effects[/i] via the Dev Agent toggle.
- Runs and backups are written under your configured session data dir: [code]synesyn/session_data_dir[/code].

[b]Safety / agency[/b]
When Dev Agent toggle is ON, the model may:
- create / modify / rename / [b]delete[/b] files (via patch apply)
- run the harness (which writes artifacts to disk)

[b]Quick start[/b]

[b]1) Set your scope[/b]
- Add the files you want the agent to edit to [i]Active Sources[/i] (SynTree main panel).
- Turn the Dev Agent toggle ON only when you're ready for side effects (patch apply/revert, harness run).

[b]2) Run a deterministic harness run[/b]
- Go to [i]Run Spec[/i]
- Pick a [b]Scene[/b] (scene_path) with [b]Browse...[/b]
- (Optional) Fill structured fields (if your project provides a schema)
- Click [b]Run[/b]

[b]3) Inspect results[/b]
- Use [b]Last harness run[/b] -> Refresh -> Open run folder
- Each run folder contains: run.json, run_spec.json, screenshot.png, ui_metrics.json, and optional logs.

[b]4) Iterate automatically[/b]
- Go to [i]Loop[/i]
- Fill [b]Goal[/b] (required), then [b]Verify[/b] (how you'll judge success)
- Click [b]Start loop[/b]

[b]Troubleshooting[/b]
- If a button seems to do nothing, check the log/result box on that tab.
- If the harness won't run: verify scene_path points to an existing .tscn.
- If structured fields are empty: set project setting [code]syntree/dev_agent/run_spec_ui_schema_path[/code] or add [code]res://syntree_run_spec_ui_schema.json[/code]."

